@ [formation_proof] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner_Formation_Consistency_Evidence_Reconciliation_Proof.sop
@ [topology_forms] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Machine_Forms.sop
@ [current_forms_revision] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Inventory_Consistency_Evidence_Revision.sop
@ [physical_plan] C:\Project\Cantor\plans\Cantor_Phase3B_3C_Physical_Proof_Plan.sop

& [ReviewIdentity] is exact
  + [review_uuid] is af32b645-91dd-4593-b84f-3a70b37155c9
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [baseline_commit] is 1835dfc467d0506bd4b068ff824a0e0eea90f282
  + [status] is checkpoint_complete_pure_acquisition_lineage_forms_selected

& [ClosedSupport] is exact
  + scanner formation now uses current evidence and receipt vocabulary
  + future non-atomic repeated equality requires two actual complete acquisition lineages, causal order, complete common scope, independent carriers, and current Equal reconciliation
  + scanner observation profile 0.1 and all unrelated formation remain inherited
  + prior formation remains historical and explicit replacement formation signature is valid
  + no implementation, runtime representation, physical producer, issuer, consumer, or execution authority exists

& [NextDependencyGap] is representation before observation
  + the canonical formation defines conceptual acquisition identities and relations but deliberately does not select bounded runtime forms
  + current TopologyReceipt contains an evidence-grade label but no acquisition support lineage
  + current supplied carriers preserve derivation ancestry but do not bind physical origin
  + a Win32 scanner implementation without strict forms would invent identities, order, scope, carrier references, and faults in code
  + physical fixtures cannot prove a protocol whose runtime evidence objects are not yet specified
  + receipt issuance cannot be safely designed before acquisition support can be represented and reviewed

& [DesignPressure] is authenticity without self-authorization
  + public serde success cannot prove actual acquisition
  + fully public constructors could let callers manufacture records that look physically observed
  + fully opaque runtime objects could become uninspectable and hard to persist in evidence
  + cryptographic signing is not automatically required for in-process provenance, but stable semantic identity and content-addressed lineage are required
  + later physical adapter construction authority must be narrower than ordinary form construction
  + pure fixture construction for tests must be visibly separate from production provenance

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] implement the full Windows scanner now
    - rejected because runtime acquisition identity, lineage ownership, causal-order representation, common-scope carrier, and fault surfaces are not canonical
  + [candidate_B] implement only low-level Win32 observation calls
    - rejected because platform facts would have no current governed acquisition envelope and could leak unsafe or partial results upward
  + [candidate_C] execute topology fixture families first
    - rejected because M2D requires a specified M2C producer and separately authorized disposable scope
  + [candidate_D] implement receipt issuance directly from current pure carriers
    - rejected because actual acquisition and causal order remain absent and form validity is not issuer proof
  + [candidate_E] add one broad M2C source containing forms, Windows seam, traversal, repetition, evidence construction, and issuance
    - rejected as too many authority and fault boundaries for one first implementation slice
  + [candidate_F] source-preserve pure bounded acquisition-lineage machine forms
    + define acquisition identity, acquisition scope, lineage references, exact completion disposition, ordered pair relation, evidence construction input, result, and faults
    + retain conceptual actual-versus-claimed distinction
    + separate ordinary decode/validation from production construction capability
    + retain exact links to current assembly, digest, reconciliation, and consistency evidence types
    + add no platform call, filesystem operation, clock read, producer, issuer, consumer, fixture, or effect

& [SelectedBoundary] is Phase3 topology acquisition lineage machine forms
  + [profile_candidate] is cantor-phase3-topology-acquisition-lineage-forms/0.1
  + [artifact_class] is strict safe-Rust pure forms only after full SJS and implementation signature
  + [candidate_module] is one new isolated cantor_ecosystem module only if later signed
  + [dependency_delta_candidate] is zero
  + [unsafe_delta_candidate] is zero
  + [effect_delta_candidate] is zero
  + [physical_authority] is absent

& [CandidateDataIdentities] require SJS, not code-first decisions
  + AcquisitionIdentity is distinct from scan nonce, digest, path, receipt hash, and ordinal
  + AcquisitionScope binds exact root, profiles, encoding, limits, policy, predecessor, and comparison coordinates
  + AcquisitionLineage references one complete current inventory and ordered digest carrier without converting it to physical truth by itself
  + AcquisitionCompletionDisposition is a closed claimed result and not proof of physical execution
  + OrderedAcquisitionPair binds two distinct acquisition identities and exact causal role relation
  + RepeatedInventoryEvidenceInput binds the pair, scope, complete carrier lineages, and current reconciliation input
  + RepeatedInventoryEvidenceResult may represent a derived claim only under a separately controlled production-construction boundary
  + typed faults distinguish invalid form, identity, scope, lineage, order, reconciliation, capability, and authority absence

& [ConstructionBoundaryQuestion] is selected for exhaustion
  + ordinary caller may decode and validate non-authoritative claim forms
  + production-grade acquisition lineage must not arise from public field construction alone
  + possible designs include private fields plus crate-confined constructors, capability-bearing producer interfaces, sealed traits, or separate claim and proven record types
  + no option is selected until semantic refinement, constraint reapplication, data design, and threat review compare inspectability, testability, forgery resistance, and future adapter integration
  + cryptographic signature, process secret, global registry, or persistence is not assumed

& [ClockAndOrderBoundary] remains abstract
  + forms may represent exact causal role and correlation without reading a clock
  + if start and completion ticks are later necessary, their domain and provenance require separate source or explicit inclusion through this source's full SJS
  + left and right remain non-temporal
  + increasing caller numbers alone never prove acquisition order

& [RelationshipToM2C] is prerequisite only
  + pure forms would let later Windows observation source declare exact outputs and faults
  + forms do not authorize a producer to construct physically authoritative records
  + later M2C must bind private construction capability to actual successful platform observation
  + later M2C must still select APIs, unsafe invariants, traversal, resources, interruption, and runtime tests

& [RelationshipToIssuance] is deferred
  + acquisition forms are support lineage, not TopologyReceipt issuance
  + later issuer must bind evidence result, receipt bytes, issuer authority, predecessor, policy, nonce, counts, and freshness
  + no receipt constructor, signer, ledger, or consumer is selected now

& [RequirementDelta] is proposed P3TALF-001 through P3TALF-014
  + exact source and predecessor binding
  + strict profile and closed serde forms
  + role-separated acquisition identity and complete scope
  + independent lineage carrier references
  + exact distinct ordered pair
  + current reconciliation binding
  + claim form versus production-construction authority separation
  + typed atomic faults and bounded validation order
  + no clock, platform, filesystem, issuer, consumer, or effect
  + adversarial construction and provenance-laundering tests
  + global, evidence, provenance, rollback, and nonclaim closure

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - no Windows API, filesystem access, traversal, acquisition execution, clock read, process, network, persistence, database, model, tool, receipt issuance, consumer, fixture, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, promotion, neural routing, distributed inference, or FPGA execution
  - no public form or test fixture may be cited as actual acquisition proof
  - no supplied carrier or Equal result may be converted directly into physical evidence
  - no code before source preservation, full SJS, data design, threat review, phase lock, and exact implementation signature

& [Decision] is source preservation before SJS
  + [next] preserve one verbose raw source for pure acquisition-lineage machine forms plus exact manifest
  + [then] audit construction authority, current type reuse, module visibility, serde need, cardinality, ordering, faults, and proof routes
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [execution_authority] is absent
  + [physical_authority] is absent
